{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And they shall stone her.</b> It is possible that after her betrothal a man lay with her, for the betrothed man did not lie with her; rather, she says she is a virgin. The transmitters of the tradition explained the matter well. These signs of virginity are found within a limited time, according to the nature of young women. And because of 'and they shall stone her,' the section of the violated woman and the betrothed woman was placed adjacent."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Reading ארם as אנם/שכב ('lay with'), following context; the word is unusual and may reflect manuscript corruption."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:24.158102651Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}